{"causes": ["The increasing accessibility of pilgrimage routes to the Holy Land in the late 15th century facilitated ambitious journeys by European elites.", "The advent of the printing press by Johannes Gutenberg in Mainz around 1450 provided the technological means for mass-producing illustrated travelogues.", "A burgeoning European interest in accurate geographic and ethnographic information about the Near East fueled demand for detailed accounts like Breydenbach's."], "effects": ["Bernhard von Breydenbach's *Peregrinatio in terram sanctam* became a foundational text for subsequent travel literature and cartography in the early modern period.", "The innovative woodcut illustrations in Breydenbach's work established new standards for visual documentation in printed books, influencing artistic and publishing practices.", "Breydenbach's detailed ethnographic observations contributed to European understanding, and often misunderstanding, of various cultures in the Near East."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "erhard-reuwich", "sourceName": "Erhard Reuwich", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "bernhard-von-breydenbach", "targetName": "Bernhard von Breydenbach", "context": "Erhard Reuwich, a Dutch artist, collaborated with Bernhard von Breydenbach by providing the detailed woodcut illustrations for his 1486 travelogue."}, {"sourceSlug": "peregrinatio-in-terram-sanctam", "sourceName": "Peregrinatio in terram sanctam", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "bernhard-von-breydenbach", "targetName": "Bernhard von Breydenbach", "context": "Bernhard von Breydenbach authored *Peregrinatio in terram sanctam*, a seminal travelogue published in 1486."}, {"sourceSlug": "bernhard-von-breydenbach", "sourceName": "Bernhard von Breydenbach", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "early-modern-cartography", "targetName": "Early Modern Cartography", "context": "Breydenbach's *Peregrinatio* significantly influenced early modern cartography through its detailed maps and city views, including the first printed bird's-eye view of Venice."}, {"sourceSlug": "bernhard-von-breydenbach", "sourceName": "Bernhard von Breydenbach", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "mainz-electorate", "targetName": "Mainz Electorate", "context": "Bernhard von Breydenbach was a politician and dean of the Mainz Cathedral Chapter within the Electorate of Mainz during the late 15th century."}, {"sourceSlug": "johannes-gutenberg", "sourceName": "Johannes Gutenberg", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "bernhard-von-breydenbach", "targetName": "Bernhard von Breydenbach", "context": "The invention of the movable type printing press by Johannes Gutenberg in Mainz enabled the widespread and illustrated publication of Breydenbach's travelogue in 1486."}], "places": [{"name": "Mainz, Holy Roman Empire", "role": "Place of Publication"}, {"name": "Jerusalem, Mamluk Sultanate", "role": "Pilgrimage Destination"}, {"name": "Venice, Republic of Venice", "role": "Journey Starting Point"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Bernhard von Breydenbach", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "bernhard-von-breydenbach"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q328688", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernhard_von_Breidenbach"], "tags": ["Explorers & Navigators", "cultural-diffusion", "environmental-history", "geopolitical-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Bernhard von Breydenbach's *Peregrinatio* was a seminal work that revolutionized travel literature and print illustration, influencing cartography and shaping European perceptions of the Near East for decades. Its detailed accounts and innovative visual elements served as an invaluable source for subsequent explorers and scholars.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-31T07:28:04Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#30611700503", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Bernhard von Breidenbach was a politician in the Electorate of Mainz. He wrote a travel report, Peregrinatio in terram sanctam (1486), from his travels to the Holy Land.", "newValue": "Bernhard von Breydenbach (died May 14, 1497) was a prominent German politician and ecclesiastic, serving as dean of the Mainz Cathedral Chapter from 1484. His enduring significance in world history stems from his authorship of *Peregrinatio in terram sanctam* (Pilgrimage to the Holy Land), published in Mainz in 1486. This foundational work of early printed travel literature documented his extensive journey to the Near East between 1483 and 1484, offering European readers an unparalleled textual and visual account of the region on the eve of the Age of Exploration.

Breydenbach embarked on his pilgrimage from Oppenheim, accompanied by several notable figures including the Dutch artist Erhard Reuwich, whose detailed woodcut illustrations transformed the *Peregrinatio* into a multimedia sensation. The expedition traveled through Venice, the Greek Isles, Cyprus, and the Holy Land, encompassing Jerusalem, Bethlehem, and the Jordan River, before venturing to Cairo and Mount Sinai. Breydenbach's narrative meticulously recorded routes, customs, flora, fauna, and local languages, providing practical advice for future pilgrims and merchants, alongside vivid descriptions of sacred sites and encounters with diverse cultures, including Greeks, Armenians, Georgians, and Mamluks.

The *Peregrinatio* achieved immediate and widespread success, being translated into German, Dutch, and French within years of its initial Latin publication. Its innovative inclusion of panoramic fold-out maps, city views (including the first printed bird's-eye view of Venice), and ethnographic illustrations set a new standard for travel accounts, influencing cartography and inspiring subsequent generations of explorers and chroniclers. The book's practical information on travel logistics, currency exchange, and local languages made it an invaluable guide, effectively democratizing access to knowledge about distant lands."}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-31T07:28:04Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#30611700503", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1440, Breidenstein"}, {"title": "Curiosity about unknown territories and navigation advances", "type": "Idea", "year": "1440, Breidenstein"}], "newValue": ["The increasing accessibility of pilgrimage routes to the Holy Land in the late 15th century facilitated ambitious journeys by European elites.", "The advent of the printing press by Johannes Gutenberg in Mainz around 1450 provided the technological means for mass-producing illustrated travelogues.", "A burgeoning European interest in accurate geographic and ethnographic information about the Near East fueled demand for detailed accounts like Breydenbach's."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-31T07:28:04Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#30611700503", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Expanded geographic knowledge and cultural exchange", "type": "Idea", "year": "1497-05-14"}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "year": "1497-05-14"}], "newValue": ["Bernhard von Breydenbach's *Peregrinatio in terram sanctam* beca